  "description": "If you want more fork travel than the Nitrous/Gila sisters, but don't want the head angle to steepen too much as a longer fork compresses, then the Scrub HTA is ready for more travel, more movement. Designed around a 140mm fork (130–150mm compatible), it pairs a 63.5° head angle with clearance for up to 29×2.8 or 27.5×2.8 tires. A low top tube increases standover and fits modern 200mm+ droppers for confident descending.\nWell executed external routing keeps cables quiet and easy to service. UDH-compatible sliders on a 148mm Boost hub adjust wheelbase up to 25mm and support all modern drivetrains, single-speed setups, and even 142mm wheels if you ask when placing the order. The beautifully reinforced stays support a 180mm rear rotor with clearance for larger brakes.",
